# Ownership for the files where a change is a trust decision rather than a
# code review. Everything else is open to normal review by anyone.
#
# CODEOWNERS only has teeth alongside branch protection on `main` with
# "Require review from Code Owners" enabled; on its own it is a suggestion.

# Workflows can reach the deploy secrets. A change here — a new trigger, an
# extra step, an unpinned action — is worth more scrutiny than the code it
# ships. `pull_request_target` in particular would expose secrets to
# pull-request code, which is how nearly every real Actions leak happens.
/.github/ @brgv-code

# The seam between the open-source build and the paid one (ADR-003, ADR-007).
# The stub's export surface is a contract with a private repository that
# reviewers here cannot see.
/packages/pro/ @brgv-code

# Entitlement and money. `users.plan` is what the paywall reads, and
# `plan_source` is what stops billing revoking a comped account (ADR-011).
/apps/api/src/routes/billing.ts @brgv-code
/apps/api/src/lib/billing.ts @brgv-code
/packages/db/migrations/ @brgv-code
